Rules: 02

Payments SDK throw = exception-native dependency at adapter seam. Caller (checkout workflow) can retry/branch/degrade on network failure, so wrap into typed `Result` (Rule 2.3, 2.5). `InvariantError` never caught to recover — rethrow unchanged if surface (Rule 2.2, profile "Translating a throwing dependency").

```ts
import { ok, err, type ResultAsync } from '@tenets/result';
import { InvariantError } from '@tenets/invariant';

type ChargeError =
	| { type: 'payments_provider_unavailable'; provider: 'stripe'; cause: unknown }
	| { type: 'payments_provider_rejected'; provider: 'stripe'; cause: unknown };

async function chargeCard(input: ChargeInput): ResultAsync<Charge, ChargeError> {
	try {
		const charge = await paymentsSdk.charge(input);
		return ok(charge);
	} catch (error) {
		if (error instanceof InvariantError) {
			throw error; // programmer bug — never laundered into recoverable error
		}
		if (isNetworkFailure(error)) {
			return err({ type: 'payments_provider_unavailable', provider: 'stripe', cause: error });
		}
		return err({ type: 'payments_provider_rejected', provider: 'stripe', cause: error });
	}
}
```

Catch once at adapter boundary, filter `InvariantError` through, translate rest to typed error carrying failure kind + provider + cause (Rule 2.5). No bare string, no untyped throw escapes past this seam (Rule 2.4).

